* MiCA in eleven cards
** What is regulated
*** Crypto-asset\n//value or right + transferable + DLT or similar//
*** E-money token (EMT)\n//one official currency → EMT, whether or not the peg holds//
*** Asset-referenced token (ART)\n//stable value, but not one currency → ART//
*** Utility token\n//access to the issuer's own good or service//
** Who must do what
*** Crypto-asset white paper\n//a document, notified not approved, instead of a licence//
*** Crypto-asset service provider (CASP)\n//ten listed services, professional basis, authorisation required//
*** Market abuse\n//listed tokens only; insider dealing, leaks, manipulation//
left side
** Who supervises
*** Competent authority\n//national supervisor; ESMA and EBA above it//
*** Passport\n//one authorisation, notify the home authority, serve the whole Union//
*** Significant token\n//three of seven criteria → stricter rules, usually EBA//
** The Regulation
*** Markets in Crypto-Assets Regulation (MiCA)\n//residual rulebook: what other EU financial law does not cover//
@endmindmap
